---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const screenshots = Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => `/assets/kababish/${String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}.jpg`);
---

<BaseLayout title="Kababish Restaurant — Case Study" description="Production Android ordering platform for a live restaurant">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <img src="/assets/kababish/logo.png" alt="Kababish" class="h-16 w-16 rounded-xl border border-strip-border object-cover" width="64" height="64" />
      <div>
        <p class="strip-label">Case Study</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold">Kababish Restaurant</h1>
        <p class="mt-1 text-strip-accent">Production Android ordering platform — v3.0.4</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {["Kotlin", "Jetpack Compose", "Supabase Realtime", "Firebase FCM", "MVVM"].map((t) => <span class="tag">{t}</span>)}
    </div>

    <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.kababish.restaurant" class="strip-btn strip-btn-primary mt-6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on Play Store</a>

    <section class="mt-12 space-y-8">
      <div class="strip-card">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-strip-signal">Context</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-strip-muted">
          Kababish, a live restaurant brand, needed a single native Android app that serves customers ordering from home and staff running kitchen operations — without juggling separate POS, delivery, and loyalty systems.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="strip-card">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-strip-accent">Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-strip-muted">
          Built with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose using MVVM architecture (a pattern that separates UI from business logic, making the app easier to test and maintain). Supabase handles authentication, database, and realtime subscriptions; Firebase delivers push notifications; PostHog tracks user behaviour. One codebase, two modes: customer ordering and role-gated admin operations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="strip-card">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-strip-warn">Solution — Customer App</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 font-data text-sm text-strip-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Full ordering system:</strong> Browse menu by category, customise items, add to cart, checkout for delivery or pickup</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Order tracking:</strong> Real-time status updates from kitchen to doorstep</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Loyalty & rewards:</strong> Earn points on orders, redeem for discounts (100 points = Rs. 50 off)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Push notifications:</strong> Order confirmations and status changes via Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Guest checkout:</strong> Order without creating an account — name, phone, and address only</li>
          <li>Voucher codes, member discounts, and offline cart persistence</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-6 text-sm font-semibold text-strip-accent">Admin Command Centre</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 font-data text-sm text-strip-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Realtime order dashboard:</strong> Live order feed with status filters (Active, Today, Yesterday, Last 7 Days), daily revenue stats, and one-tap status updates — kitchen screen stays awake</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Menu management:</strong> Toggle item availability and manage inventory without redeploying the app</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Discount management:</strong> Configure global discount rules and member pricing from the admin panel</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Delivery management:</strong> Global delivery on/off toggle, area-based delivery fees, and per-zone pricing control</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Notifications panel:</strong> Push new orders to kitchen devices instantly; tap a notification to jump directly to the relevant order</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">UI customisation:</strong> Update homepage carousel images and category visuals at runtime — no app store update needed</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Support tickets:</strong> Handle customer issues from within the admin shell</li>
          <li><strong class="text-strip-text">Realtime sync:</strong> Supabase subscriptions push order changes to every connected admin and customer device within seconds</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="strip-card">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-strip-text">Effect</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-strip-muted">
          A live Android application (v3.0.4 on Google Play) that replaces fragmented restaurant tooling with one end-to-end system. Customers order, track, and earn rewards from their phone; staff manage the full order lifecycle in realtime from a dedicated admin dashboard — menu, pricing, delivery, and notifications all configurable without code changes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Screenshots</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4">
        {screenshots.map((src, i) => (
          <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-strip-border">
            <img src={src} alt={`Kababish screenshot ${i + 1}`} class="aspect-[9/19] w-full object-cover object-top" loading="lazy" />
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
